--
`return {r}` into an aggregate with a non-POD member only tries
constructor candidates ([stmt.return]/2 requires copy-list-init, which
for aggregates is aggregate initialization).  Non-return braced init of
the same class works.  Blocks dog-fooding
restrict_function_pointers.cpp.
